  "offerings": [
    {
      "uuid": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
      "name": "Basic VM",
      "type": "Marketplace.Basic",
      "state": 2,
      "shared": true,
      "billable": true,
      "category_uuid": "cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc",
      "customer_uuid": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
      "description": "Basic virtual machine offering with CPU, RAM, and storage components",
      "plugin_options": {
        "service_provider_can_create_offering_user": true
      },
      "getting_started": "## Getting Started with Basic VM\n\n1. **Connect via SSH**: Use your SSH key to connect to your VM\n   ```\n   ssh user@<vm-ip-address>\n   ```\n\n2. **Check system resources**: Verify your allocated CPU, RAM, and storage\n   ```\n   cat /proc/cpuinfo | grep processor | wc -l\n   free -h\n   df -h\n   ```\n\n3. **Install software**: Update packages and install what you need\n   ```\n   sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y\n   ```\n\nFor support, contact support@demo.waldur.com"
    },
    {
      "uuid": "00000000000000000000000000000010",
      "name": "Block Storage",
      "type": "Marketplace.Basic",
      "state": 2,
      "shared": true,
      "billable": true,
      "category_uuid": "dddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddd",
      "customer_uuid": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
      "description": "Block storage volumes with configurable size",
      "getting_started": "## Getting Started with Block Storage\n\n1. **Attach the volume**: The storage volume will be attached to your VM as a new device\n\n2. **Format the volume** (first time only):\n   ```\n   sudo mkfs.ext4 /dev/vdb\n   ```\n\n3. **Mount the volume**:\n   ```\n   sudo mkdir -p /mnt/data\n   sudo mount /dev/vdb /mnt/data\n   ```\n\n4. **Make it persistent**: Add to /etc/fstab for automatic mounting on reboot\n\nFor support, contact support@demo.waldur.com"
    },
    {
      "uuid": "08500000000000000000000000000010",
      "name": "Kubernetes Cluster (Single Datacenter)",
      "type": "Support.OfferingTemplate",
      "state": 2,
      "shared": true,
      "billable": true,
      "category_uuid": "cdef0123456789abcdef012345678901",
      "customer_uuid": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
      "description": "Production-ready Kubernetes cluster deployed in a single datacenter with automated provisioning, monitoring, and scaling capabilities.",
      "options": {
        "order": [
          "cluster_config"
        ],
        "options": {
          "cluster_config": {
            "type": "single_datacenter_085_config",
            "label": "Cluster Configuration",
            "help_text": "Configure your Kubernetes cluster including controller nodes, load balancers, and worker node groups",
            "required": true,
            "default_configs": {
              "default_controller_vcpus": 4,
              "default_controller_ram_gb": 8,
              "default_controller_system_disk_gb": 50,
              "default_controller_etcd_disk_gb": 20,
              "default_lb_vcpus": 2,
              "default_lb_ram_gb": 4,
              "default_lb_system_disk_gb": 20,
              "default_lb_logs_disk_gb": 50,
              "minimal_worker_vcpus": 2,
              "minimal_worker_ram_gb": 4,
              "default_worker_data_disk_gb": 100,
              "default_storage_data_disk_gb": 200,
              "default_storage_san_disk_gb": 500,
              "available_kubernetes_versions": "1.28.0,1.29.0,1.30.0"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "plugin_options": {
        "backend_type": "085-single-dc",
        "service_type": "kubernetes-cluster",
        "deployment_mode": "managed",
        "service_provider_can_create_offering_user": true
      },
      "getting_started": "## Getting Started with Kubernetes Cluster\n\n1. **Access the cluster**:\n   Download your kubeconfig from the resource details page\n   ```\n   export KUBECONFIG=~/Downloads/kubeconfig.yaml\n   kubectl get nodes\n   ```\n\n2. **Deploy an application**:\n   ```\n   kubectl create deployment nginx --image=nginx\n   kubectl expose deployment nginx --port=80 --type=LoadBalancer\n   ```\n\n3. **Monitor your cluster**:\n   Access Grafana dashboard from the endpoints section\n\nFor support, contact support@demo.waldur.com"
    },
