      "plugin_options": {
        "backend_type": "085-multi-dc",
        "service_type": "kubernetes-cluster",
        "deployment_mode": "managed",
        "high_availability": true,
        "service_provider_can_create_offering_user": true
      },
      "getting_started": "## Getting Started with Multi-Datacenter Kubernetes Cluster\n\n1. **Access the cluster**:\n   Download your kubeconfig from the resource details page\n   ```\n   export KUBECONFIG=~/Downloads/kubeconfig.yaml\n   kubectl get nodes -o wide\n   ```\n\n2. **View datacenter distribution**:\n   ```\n   kubectl get nodes --label-columns=topology.kubernetes.io/zone\n   ```\n\n3. **Deploy a geo-distributed application**:\n   ```\n   kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes/examples/master/guestbook/all-in-one/guestbook-all-in-one.yaml\n   ```\n\n4. **Monitor cluster health**:\n   Access the federation dashboard from the endpoints section\n\nFor support, contact support@demo.waldur.com"
    },
